.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt E2FSCK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm e2fsck
.Nd check and repair an ext2 file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl pacnyrdfkvtDFV
.Op Fl b Ar superblock
.Op Fl B Ar blocksize
.Op Fl l Ns | Ns Fl L Ar bad_blocks_file
.Op Fl C Ar fd
.Op Fl E Ar extended_options
.Op Fl z Ar undo_file
.Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks and repairs the ext2 file system on
.Ar device ,
a partition node such as
.Pa /dev/disk0p3 .
The volume must be unmounted.
The recovery system mounts nothing from the disk it repairs.
Rach2 volumes use ext2 without a journal, so journal recovery does not
run on them.
.Pp
Rach2 uses e2fsprogs 1.47.4, linked statically against the ported musl.
.Nm
is installed only in the recovery image, at
.Pa /sbin/e2fsck ;
os-real and the installed root do not include it.
The build includes libuuid and libblkid and disables NLS, thread-local
storage, uuidd, fuse2fs, e2initrd-helper, e2image, e4defrag, debugfs,
multi-mount protection, backtraces, and tdb.
Only
.Nm
and
.Xr resize2fs 8
are built as guest e2fsprogs programs.
No e2fsprogs volume formatter or manual editor is installed.
.Pp
The partition nodes provide raw sector access.
The library uses whole 512-byte sectors at sector-aligned offsets,
with a bounce buffer for partial-sector I/O, and obtains the device
size through
.Ql BLKGETSIZE64 .
The recovery image's
.Pa /etc/mtab
is empty, so that file does not identify mounted volumes.
Do not run
.Nm
on a mounted volume.
.Pp
The repair modes
.Fl p
.Pq or Fl a ,
.Fl n ,
and
.Fl y
are mutually exclusive.
Without one of these modes,
.Nm
requires a terminal for interactive repairs.
.Ss Use by recovery programs
When the boot line includes
.Ql rach2.fsck ,
init runs
.Ql e2fsck -p
on each partition from
.Pa /dev/disk0p1
through
.Pa /dev/disk0p4
whose superblock has the ext2 magic number.
It records the result as:
.Dl init: e2fsck: /dev/disk0pN: status S
See
.Xr recovery 7 .
.Pp
Menu entry 2 of
.Xr rach2-recover 8
runs
.Ql e2fsck -f -n DEVICE .
On a nonzero status it reports
.Ql e2fsck -f -p DEVICE
as the repair command, without running it.
.Pp
.Xr growroot 8
first runs
.Ql e2fsck -f -n
and stops on a nonzero status.
It then runs
.Ql e2fsck -f -p
and accepts statuses 0, 1, and 2 before running
.Xr resize2fs 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Same as
.Fl p ;
retained for compatibility.
.It Fl b Ar superblock
Use the specified backup superblock instead of the primary superblock.
Its location depends on the block size, blocks per group, and file
system features.
Unless opened read-only, the primary superblock is updated when the
check finishes.
.It Fl B Ar blocksize
Search for the superblock using only this block size.
Failure to find it is a fatal error.
.It Fl c
Run badblocks to scan for bad blocks and add them to the bad block inode.
One occurrence requests a read-only scan; two request a nondestructive
read-write scan.
No badblocks program is installed on Rach2, so this option fails to run it.
.It Fl C Ar fd
Write progress information to the specified descriptor.
A negative value selects its absolute value and initially suppresses
progress; SIGUSR1 enables it.
.Fl C Cm 0
displays a completion bar on the terminal.
.It Fl d
Print debugging output.
.It Fl D
Optimize all directories by re-indexing them, or by sorting and
compressing linear directories.
Also check for duplicate names within a directory.
.It Fl E Ar extended_options
Set comma-separated extended options.
An option's argument follows an equals sign.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql ea_ver=version
Require extended attribute block version 1 or 2; the default is 2.
.It Ql journal_only
Replay the journal if needed, without further checks or repairs.
Rach2 ext2 volumes have no journal.
.It Ql fragcheck
Report discontiguous file blocks during pass 1.
.It Ql discard
Attempt to discard free blocks and unused inode blocks after the full
check, in pass 5, if the check finds no remaining errors.
Discarding can prevent later manual recovery of undetected damage.
.It Ql nodiscard
Do not discard free blocks or unused inode blocks.
This is the default.
.It Ql no_optimize_extents
Do not offer to reduce the width or depth of extent trees.
.It Ql optimize_extents
Offer to reduce the width or depth of extent trees.
This is the default unless changed in
.Pa /etc/e2fsck.conf .
.It Ql inode_count_fullmap
Use additional memory to speed checks of file systems with many hard
links.
Memory use is proportional to the inode count.
.It Ql no_inode_count_fullmap
Disable that optimization.
This is the default unless changed in
.Pa /etc/e2fsck.conf .
.It Ql readahead_kb=value
Use the specified number of KiB to prefetch metadata.
Zero disables readahead.
The default is the size of two block groups' inode tables;
readahead is disabled if that exceeds 1/50 of physical memory.
.It Ql bmap2extent
Convert block-mapped files to extent-mapped files.
.It Ql fixes_only
Repair damaged metadata without optimizing directory indexes or
compressing extent trees.
Incompatible with
.Fl D
and
.Fl E Cm bmap2extent .
.It Ql check_encoding
Verify encoded names in case-insensitive directories.
This is the default when the file system's strict flag is set.
.It Ql unshare_blocks
Copy shared blocks and clear the shared-blocks read-only feature.
Without that feature, this option has no effect.
Insufficient free space causes failure without an offer to delete files.
This option implies
.Fl f .
With
.Fl n ,
simulate the required allocation and return a nonzero status if it fails.
.El
.It Fl f
Check even a file system marked clean.
.It Fl F
Flush the device's buffer cache before checking.
.It Fl k
With
.Fl c ,
retain the existing bad blocks list and add any newly found bad blocks.
.It Fl l Ar bad_blocks_file
Add the block numbers in the file to the bad blocks list.
The file uses badblocks output format, with block numbers in units of
the file system's block size.
.It Fl L Ar bad_blocks_file
Replace the bad blocks list with the block numbers in the file.
.It Fl n
Open read-only and answer no to every question.
Nothing is written to the volume.
.It Fl p
Repair automatically what can be safely repaired without a person's
intervention.
Ask no questions.
If further action is needed, describe the problem and include 4 in the
exit status.
.It Fl r
Do nothing; retained for compatibility.
.It Fl t
Print timing statistics.
Specify twice for statistics for each pass.
.It Fl v
Print verbose output.
.It Fl V
Print version information and exit.
.It Fl y
Answer yes to every question.
.It Fl z Ar undo_file
Save each block's old contents in an undo file before overwriting it.
An empty argument selects
.Pa e2fsck-device.e2undo
in the directory specified by
.Ev E2FSPROGS_UNDO_DIR ,
with
.Ql device
replaced by the device name.
The undo file cannot recover from a power failure or system crash.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/e2fsck.conf
.It Pa /sbin/e2fsck
The recovery image's checker.
.It Pa /etc/mtab
Empty mount table in the recovery image.
.It Pa /etc/e2fsck.conf
Configuration file; absent from the recovery image.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status is the sum of the applicable values:
.Bl -tag -width 128 -compact
.It 0
No errors.
.It 1
File system errors corrected.
.It 2
File system errors corrected; the system should be rebooted.
.It 4
File system errors left uncorrected.
.It 8
Operational error.
.It 16
Usage or syntax error.
.It 32
Cancelled by the user.
.It 128
Shared library error; not applicable to the static Rach2 build.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check the root partition without writing, from an SSH session on the
recovery system:
.Dl e2fsck -fn /dev/disk0p3
.Pp
In the source tree,
.Ql tests/run grow
runs the read-only and repairing checks through
.Xr growroot 8 .
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Conflicting repair modes produce:
.Dl Only one of the options -p/-a, -n or -y may be specified.
An interactive run without a terminal reports:
.Dl need terminal for interactive repairs
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr disk 7 ,
.Xr recovery 7 ,
.Xr growroot 8 ,
.Xr rach2-recover 8 ,
.Xr resize2fs 8
